# Yazi — terminal file manager

## Launch
    yy        # open yazi and cd to wherever you quit (shell wrapper)
    yazi      # open yazi, return to original directory on quit

## Navigation
    h / l     # parent / enter directory (or open file)
    j / k     # down / up
    H / L     # back / forward in history
    g g       # jump to top
    G         # jump to bottom
    .         # toggle hidden files

## Jump
    z         # zoxide jump (fuzzy, uses your zoxide history)
    Z         # zoxide jump scoped to current directory

## Selection & operations
    Space     # select/deselect file
    v         # visual (bulk select)
    y         # yank (copy)
    x         # cut
    p         # paste
    d         # trash
    D         # delete permanently
    a         # create file or directory (trailing / = directory)
    r         # rename

## Search
    /         # filter files in current directory
    s         # search file contents (requires ripgrep)
    S         # search filenames (requires fd)

## Open
    Enter     # open with default opener (nvim for text, open/xdg-open otherwise)
    o         # open with custom picker

## Theme
    Catppuccin Mocha (matches bat, ghostty)
